      <h2>About Old Fort</h2>
      <div>Ngome Kongwe (Old Fort) is the oldest surviving building in Stone Town, built by Omani Arabs in the late 17th century on the foundations of a Portuguese chapel. The massive coral stone walls with castellated towers have served as a garrison, prison, and marketplace over three centuries. Today it houses a cultural center with artisan shops, an open-air amphitheater hosting taarab and ngoma performances, and the Zanzibar Cultural Arts Centre. Free entry; rooftop offers panoramic views of the harbor and Forodhani Gardens.</div>
